  note    = {"Rat and monkey Kp,uu,brain-values were highly correlated (R^2=0.74; n=17). Based on this finding a correlation between rat and human Kp,uu,brain was expected. However, no correlation between rat and human Kp,uu,brain was found (R^2=0.01; n=13). [...] Results indicate that available human Kp,uu,brain-data are too uncertain to be applicable for validation of predictions and understanding of clinical brain uptake of drugs and drug candidates" (abstract, bioRxiv API record api.biorxiv.org/details/biorxiv/10.1101/2022.11.14.516429, read 13 October 2026). The only direct rat-to-human Kp,uu,brain comparison found; qualification 2 of route 3 in docs/brain_exposure_data_feasibility.md, and a caution that applies equally to the 89 largely-rodent values this repository already holds. A PREPRINT, not peer reviewed, by an author at a company selling the prediction software used in it, on 13 compounds: reported, not relied on. CC BY-ND per the provider's machine-readable field ("license":"cc_by_nd"), not read as prose because bioRxiv's robots file disallows the article page to automated readers; the per-drug tables are the owner's to open}
}

